{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>And I will be glorified through Pharaoh.</b> When the Holy One, blessed be He, takes vengeance on the wicked, His name is magnified and glorified. And so it says: ״וְנִשְׁפַּטְתִּי אִתּוֹ וְגוֹ׳״ — and afterward: ״וְהִתְגַּדִּלְתִּי וְהִתְקַדִּשְׁתִּי וְנוֹדַעְתִּי וְגוֹ׳״ (Ezekiel 38). And it says: ״שָׁם שִׁבַּר רִשְׁפֵי קֶשֶׁת״ — and afterward: ״נוֹדָע בִּיהוּדָה אֱלֹהִים״ (Psalms 76). And it says: ״נוֹדַע ה׳ מִשְׁפָּט עָשָׂה״ (ibid. 9)." "<b>Through Pharaoh and through all his army.</b> He began the transgression, and from him the punishment began." "<b>And they did so.</b> To declare their praise — that they listened to the voice of Moses and did not say, How shall we approach our pursuers? We need to flee! — but they said: We have only to fulfill the words of the son of Amram (Mekhilta)."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:52:05.908905146Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}